            "description": "The same request as step 5, made by someone who was never nominated for this account.\n\nStep 5 returns a subject token. This returns an error and no token.\n\nOut of the box the Identity Server would allow this - its own validator only checks that the caller holds the impersonation scope, which step 10 shows they do. The nomination check is what refuses it."
